  "caption": "Quinn saw a side-on photo, spotted a question-mark shape, and ordered a posture brace. Problem solved? Not quite.\n\nSome upper-back rounding can improve with strength and mobility work, but bony shape won't reverse, and braces don't reshape the curve.\n\nWhat often helps: strengthen your back extensors with arm raises, rows and gentle back extensions, mobilise your mid-back over a foam roller, keep up general resistance training, and do frequent, gentle posture resets through the day.\n\nIf you get sudden mid-back pain, notice you've lost more than a couple of centimetres in height, or have a risk of osteoporosis, see your GP first.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
